Z||000000||donalson||09-11-2001||02:56 AM||||i know many dif swaps have been done to the fiero...<P>whats the advantages of the quad 4?...what kinda output does it have?...how revy is it (sorry i love to rev...my '86 gets reved to 7500 daily) <P>what v-6s are worth putting into the fiero?...<P>i'm just asking cause i was told that the 6 was the way to go for an auto-x/track car (street legal still)<P>thanks<BR>mark||||reg||1
Z||000001||87FieroGTx||09-11-2001||04:04 AM|||| For autoX I would go Q4 all the way, With the Q4 you will have 50/50 weight and with the Turbo kit they can make 325hp. <P> Oh and they were made to REVVVVV...<P> If you want Drag race power go for a 3.8 V-6 or a V-8||||reg||1
Z||000002||donalson||09-11-2001||04:37 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87FieroGTx:<BR><B> For autoX I would go Q4 all the way, With the Q4 you will have 50/50 weight and with the Turbo kit they can make 325hp. <P> Oh and they were made to REVVVVV...<P> If you want Drag race power go for a 3.8 V-6 or a V-8</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>what kinda reliable power can they put out?...how much are turbo kits for em?...how much are the engines?<P>anyone got any dyno's of a turbo quad4<P>wheres redline on em  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>and i like 50/50  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">...curves and cones baby  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>'86 mr2 hardtop<P>mid-engine lover||||reg||1
Z||000003||HummelHund||09-11-2001||10:43 PM||||I don't know about the turbo versions, but naturally aspirated factory high output versions were putting out 180hp in certain GM models. I have heard that the early Quad-4's ate head gaskets but that later models were improved so that didn't happen. I *think* the redline was somewhere in the vicinity of 7000rpm, but I may be wrong (as is often the case). <BR><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE, The "Buzz Bomb". (restoration project/daily driver)<BR>'84 SE (Dad's Project)||||reg||1
Z||000004||Philphine||09-12-2001||08:17 AM||||a few months back quite a few of the mags (possibly under one publishing co.)  were running articles on how to mix and match quad 4 parts with newer dohc engines (like in the sunbird/cavalier. don't remember what they call it now) for better reliability and performance.<P>a 4 cam 3.4 might also work if you want revability.<P>northstar?||||reg||1
Z||000005||artherd||09-13-2001||06:37 AM||||Quad4 will make for a very light fiero (I don't know about handling with a 50/50 bias mid-engine car.  it shouldn't really be different, but it will depend on where the real polar moments are, not just tyre weight.<P>3.4TDC will make a very nice Fiero, it will safely rev to 7grand and do so reliably (many stock fordged components!!)<P>I'm going with a Northstar.  Wanna know how to make a Northstar rev to 8grand?  change the cams, valve springs, and lifters.   You can almost do it with the engine still in the car (just pull heads, prolly easier out though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I will probally break a carburator bearing or three though, time will tell!<P><BR>You can't really go wrong with any of these 4-cam GM engines, they're amazingly good motors and any are LOTS of fun in a Fiero!!<P><BR>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
